  "body": {
    "id": "thm:crossfit-attainment",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "After correcting the ratio score and the influence-value variance estimator, the stated cross-fitted estimator is asymptotically linear with influence function \\(b^\\star(X)'\\Psi_P(O)\\) and its pointwise Wald interval is valid under the displayed rate and positivity conditions.  It attains the minimum variance in the aggregate pairwise-score family.  It is semiparametrically efficient only in submodels for which the aggregate comparison closure equals the full period-specific tangent normal closure.",
